# car: the flow of depot yardr's cars. A car is one piece of a train, built
# in parallel with its siblings: the builder gates it with the depot's light
# gate (.yardr/check-light: only what it changed and what imports that is
# tested), the refinery lands it on the train's
# branch under the same light gate, and nobody reviews it by itself. The full
# gate and the one review are the train's, on the whole, before main moves
# (yardr.train.flow). So there is no review stage here. A car with no train
# never leaves backlog: yardr refuses the move. See docs/pipeline.md#cars.
backlog -> new
new -> approved on done | decide on question | backlog
approved -> merged on done | new on failed | decide on question
decide -> backlog | new
merged terminal
